# Supplemental objc2 family license notices

The crates below declare MIT (or MIT as an alternative) in their published
Cargo manifests, but their crates.io archives do not include a license text.
Their upstream repository's LICENSE.md at each source commit confirms this
licensing scope. We retain the upstream MIT text and scope notice from commit
8a5abacd90d5403fc0463459a35826f892b9142e (2026-10-17):

- https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2/blob/8a5abacd90d5403fc0463459a35826f892b9142e/LICENSE-MIT.txt
- https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2/blob/8a5abacd90d5403fc0463459a35826f892b9142e/LICENSE.md

These are upstream notices, not a license newly granted by CharArt.rs.
The 2026 MIT text supplements the declarations in the older crate archives;
it is not claimed to have been included in those original archives.

